{
  "id": "s02-l01",
  "unit": "s02-consonants",
  "title": "Consonants 1: ক খ গ ঘ ঙ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Consonants (ব্যঞ্জনবর্ণ byænjonborno) come in rows of five**, ordered from the back of the mouth to the lips. Row 1 is made in the throat: **ক খ গ ঘ ঙ**.\n\n**Every consonant has a built-in vowel `o`.** On its own, ক is read `ko`. At the end of a word that `o` usually goes silent: ঘর is `ghor`, not *ghoro*.\n\n**Aspiration is a real difference.** খ (`kh`) and ঘ (`gh`) are ক and গ with a puff of air; hold a hand in front of your mouth to feel it. ক is like the k in *skin* (no puff). Getting this wrong changes words, so listen closely.\n\n**ঙ** (`ng` as in *sing*) never starts a word and sounds just like the sign ং, which you'll meet in s02-l07.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-ka",
      "bn": "ক",
      "tr": "ko",
      "en": "k as in 'skin' (no puff of air)",
      "notes": "Name: ko (ক). First letter of কেমন and কী."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-kha",
      "bn": "খ",
      "tr": "kho",
      "en": "kh: k with a puff of air, as in 'kite'",
      "notes": "Name: kho (খ). The aspirated partner of ক."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ga",
      "bn": "গ",
      "tr": "go",
      "en": "g as in 'go'",
      "notes": "Name: go (গ)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-gha",
      "bn": "ঘ",
      "tr": "gho",
      "en": "gh: g with a breathy puff",
      "notes": "Name: gho (ঘ). The aspirated partner of গ."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-nga",
      "bn": "ঙ",
      "tr": "ng",
      "en": "ng as in 'sing' (never starts a word)",
      "notes": "Name: ungo (উঙ). Same sound as the sign ং (s02-l07); only the spelling differs. Main use is inside conjuncts like ঙ্গ (লুঙ্গি)."
    },
    {
      "id": "gachh",
      "bn": "গাছ",
      "tr": "gachh",
      "en": "tree"
    },
    {
      "id": "goru",
      "bn": "গরু",
      "tr": "goru",
      "en": "cow"
    },
    {
      "id": "ghor",
      "bn": "ঘর",
      "tr": "ghor",
      "en": "room / house",
      "notes": "Also 'home' in a general sense; বাড়ি (bari) is the usual word for a house/home."
    },
    {
      "id": "bangali",
      "bn": "বাঙালি",
      "tr": "bangali",
      "en": "Bengali (person)",
      "notes": "Example of ঙ inside a word. Bangla Academy standard: colour is spelled রং on its own, রঙ only before an ending (রঙিন)."
    }
  ],
